window.SCHOOL_LISTENING={"../assets/media/6fd93a8c4baaf5d14e28bce8b3a1ec1e2d99eb57f241e04d230e333302e56647.mp3":[{"id":"PPT_6fd93a8c4baaf5d1","audioId":"PPT_6fd93a8c4baaf5d1","title":"Book 2 · Unit 5 · LS · LISTENING 1","subtitle":"LISTENING 1 · source slide 32","duration":48.09,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.48,"text":"Unit five,","coverage":1},{"start":2.1,"end":3.12,"text":"five .one","coverage":1},{"start":4.78,"end":5.64,"text":"one","coverage":1},{"start":6.51,"end":9.42,"text":"The teacher's name isn't Mr Rosso,","coverage":1},{"start":9.84,"end":11.46,"text":"it's Mr Rosson.","coverage":1},{"start":13.66,"end":14.52,"text":"two","coverage":1},{"start":15.41,"end":17.12,"text":"I had a golf lesson,","coverage":1},{"start":17.62,"end":19,"text":"not a tennis lesson.","coverage":1},{"start":21.3,"end":22.16,"text":"three","coverage":1},{"start":23.12,"end":26.86,"text":"The match is at six tonight, not six .30,","coverage":1},{"start":27.04,"end":28.22,"text":"so don't be late.","coverage":1},{"start":30.38,"end":31.4,"text":"four","coverage":1},{"start":32.56,"end":34.98,"text":"Yasmin doesn't do drama classes,","coverage":1},{"start":35.6,"end":37.86,"text":"she does gymnastics classes.","coverage":1},{"start":40.4,"end":41.42,"text":"five","coverage":1},{"start":42.11,"end":44.52,"text":"The competition will be in Colombia,","coverage":1},{"start":45.12,"end":46.16,"text":"not in Brazil.","coverage":1}],"file":"09f85c3b100bf4e7dd30.js","track":0,"media":"../assets/media/6fd93a8c4baaf5d14e28bce8b3a1ec1e2d99eb57f241e04d230e333302e56647.mp3"}],"../assets/media/d7d40bf5985e4eed388a86371a8d70b5bf9eda02a5eede4c64cc9d718f4f85b7.mp3":[{"id":"PPT_d7d40bf5985e4eed","audioId":"PPT_d7d40bf5985e4eed","title":"Book 2 · Unit 5 · LS · LISTENING 1","subtitle":"LISTENING 1 · source slide 54","duration":244.92,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.7,"text":"five .two","coverage":1},{"start":2.74,"end":4.56,"text":"For my project,","coverage":1},{"start":4.96,"end":9.8,"text":"I looked at some unusual sports that people play around the world.","coverage":1},{"start":10.42,"end":14.48,"text":"I'd like to start by talking about chess boxing.","coverage":1},{"start":15.42,"end":18.02,"text":"You may already know about the two sports.","coverage":1},{"start":18.7,"end":23.18,"text":"Chess is a game played with a board and different chess pieces.","coverage":1},{"start":23.18,"end":31.57,"text":"Very intelligent people often play this game because players need to think very carefully.","coverage":1},{"start":32.92,"end":36.8,"text":"Boxing is a totally different kind of sport though.","coverage":1},{"start":37.76,"end":43.16,"text":"Being strong is more important because boxers have to hit each other.","coverage":1},{"start":43.94,"end":49.28,"text":"They wear gloves and helmets in the ring, but it's still difficult.","coverage":1},{"start":50.24,"end":51.16,"text":"Now,","coverage":1},{"start":51.6,"end":58.1,"text":"chess boxing is a new type of sport where the players do both activities.","coverage":1},{"start":59.08,"end":60.54,"text":"They start with boxing,","coverage":1},{"start":60.9,"end":61.32,"text":"sorry,","coverage":1},{"start":61.8,"end":63.24,"text":"I mean chess,","coverage":1},{"start":63.98,"end":65.6,"text":"and then do some boxing,","coverage":1},{"start":66.12,"end":71.32,"text":"and they continue doing each activity back and forth, alternating.","coverage":1},{"start":72.54,"end":78.74,"text":"The person who wins the boxing match or the chess game first is the champion.","coverage":1},{"start":79.28,"end":87.72,"text":"One benefit of this sport is that it gives people a chance to compete physically and mentally.","coverage":1},{"start":88.76,"end":91.68,"text":"It isn't just thinking or physical activity.","coverage":1},{"start":92.4,"end":93.32,"text":"It's both.","coverage":1},{"start":95.46,"end":99.44,"text":"Another sport that challenges people is urban golf.","coverage":1},{"start":100.12,"end":103.44,"text":"Urban golf is similar to normal golf,","coverage":1},{"start":103.78,"end":107.02,"text":"but you don't need to go to a golf course.","coverage":1},{"start":107.02,"end":110.92,"text":"You get clubs and a golf ball.","coverage":1},{"start":111.4,"end":111.92,"text":"Well,","coverage":1},{"start":112.24,"end":112.86,"text":"actually,","coverage":1},{"start":113.44,"end":117.46,"text":"it's a soft tennis ball instead of a hard golf ball.","coverage":1},{"start":118,"end":120.86,"text":"Then you can play in the street,","coverage":1},{"start":121.26,"end":123.29,"text":"which is why it's called urban.","coverage":1},{"start":124.64,"end":126.44,"text":"If you play urban golf,","coverage":1},{"start":126.92,"end":131.18,"text":"you don't need to go anywhere special or need much money to play.","coverage":1},{"start":131.76,"end":134.82,"text":"You just agree where you want to hit the ball.","coverage":1},{"start":134.82,"end":136.16,"text":"For example,","coverage":1},{"start":136.54,"end":139.32,"text":"at a sign in the street or a rubbish bin.","coverage":1},{"start":140.24,"end":141.46,"text":"On the other hand,","coverage":1},{"start":142.16,"end":147.84,"text":"intelligent players know that you may break something if you hit the ball too hard,","coverage":1},{"start":148.16,"end":150.94,"text":"so they try to play fairly carefully.","coverage":1},{"start":153.06,"end":153.74,"text":"Next,","coverage":1},{"start":154.16,"end":165,"text":"I'd like to talk about the Moroccan desert footrace, which is also called the Marathon des Sables or the Tahara Marathon.","coverage":1},{"start":166.32,"end":173.12,"text":"This race is held every year over a week or rather over six days.","coverage":1},{"start":174.26,"end":177.1,"text":"The runners have to be really strong.","coverage":1},{"start":177.86,"end":179.42,"text":"On the longest day,","coverage":1},{"start":179.72,"end":182.74,"text":"the runners have to run 92 kilometers.","coverage":1},{"start":183.76,"end":192.98,"text":"The best thing about it is that the champion can say he or she has won the hardest marathon in the world.","coverage":1},{"start":194.12,"end":194.44,"text":"Finally,","coverage":1},{"start":195.12,"end":198.38,"text":"I'd like to look at Sepak Takraw.","coverage":1},{"start":199.3,"end":204.83,"text":"This is a type of volleyball and is very popular in Southeast Asia.","coverage":1},{"start":206.28,"end":216.06,"text":"The players use a different kind of ball, and they can use their feet to kick the ball or hit it with their knees, chest or head.","coverage":1},{"start":217.22,"end":221.7,"text":"The sport began in Indonesia and it, no,","coverage":1},{"start":222.06,"end":222.94,"text":"not Indonesia,","coverage":1},{"start":223.58,"end":225.78,"text":"it began in Malaysia,","coverage":1},{"start":226.78,"end":231.26,"text":"although it is also very popular in Thailand and Indonesia.","coverage":1},{"start":232.18,"end":240.5,"text":"One good thing about Sepak Takraw is that it is now played in schools in many countries, including Japan,","coverage":1},{"start":240.9,"end":242.98,"text":"and gets children to play sport.","coverage":1}],"file":"4ab2ba09157118519ff9.js","track":0,"media":"../assets/media/d7d40bf5985e4eed388a86371a8d70b5bf9eda02a5eede4c64cc9d718f4f85b7.mp3"}],"../assets/media/d03378d2ce6264fc09340a9807bf5ddb3bdb18eab63cfbca14309bd008cc5b01.mp3":[{"id":"PPT_d03378d2ce6264fc","audioId":"PPT_d03378d2ce6264fc","title":"Book 2 · Unit 5 · LS · LISTENING 2","subtitle":"LISTENING 2 · source slide 90","duration":293.8,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1,"text":"five .five","coverage":1},{"start":3.44,"end":8.34,"text":"Andre, I know you played in a university football team in the US,","coverage":1},{"start":8.76,"end":11.74,"text":"so I'd like to ask your opinion about something.","coverage":1},{"start":12.7,"end":18.44,"text":"Do you think the Olympic athletes and other athletes, like football and tennis players,","coverage":1},{"start":18.96,"end":21.7,"text":"are too focused on getting money from companies?","coverage":1},{"start":22.34,"end":24.38,"text":"I went on holiday in","coverage":1},{"start":25.24,"end":28.02,"text":"and every time I turned on the TV,","coverage":1},{"start":28.44,"end":31.86,"text":"I saw a famous athlete in an advert for some product.","coverage":1},{"start":33.14,"end":37.46,"text":"Those athletes are getting paid a huge amount of money to be in adverts.","coverage":1},{"start":38.32,"end":44.1,"text":"It seems like the athletes are more interested in making money than in representing their countries.","coverage":1},{"start":45.32,"end":50.6,"text":"I think there is definitely more marketing and business in sport than ever before.","coverage":1},{"start":51.5,"end":52.56,"text":"As a long -time","coverage":1},{"start":53.12,"end":61.56,"text":"I really think all this money and advertising from big companies is taking something away from sports and competitions.","coverage":1},{"start":62.54,"end":64.96,"text":"Well, I would say that all athletes,","coverage":1},{"start":65.38,"end":69.66,"text":"even the rich and famous ones, are still very focused on the sport.","coverage":1},{"start":70.44,"end":71.42,"text":"Without the sport,","coverage":1},{"start":71.8,"end":72.22,"text":"they have","coverage":1},{"start":72.22,"end":72.44,"text":"no","coverage":1},{"start":72.44,"end":72.86,"text":"job.","coverage":1},{"start":73.78,"end":78,"text":"And athletes who aren't famous, or are only a little famous,","coverage":1},{"start":78.7,"end":80.66,"text":"deserve to make all the money they can.","coverage":1},{"start":81.36,"end":84.48,"text":"Many athletes devote their whole lives to training.","coverage":1},{"start":85.24,"end":89.18,"text":"How can they live, work, and pay for coaching all by themselves?","coverage":1},{"start":90.46,"end":91.44,"text":"Being an athlete,","coverage":1},{"start":91.98,"end":93.92,"text":"especially one who doesn't get paid,","coverage":1},{"start":94.34,"end":95.94,"text":"is extremely expensive.","coverage":1},{"start":96.8,"end":99.08,"text":"The cost of training is really high,","coverage":1},{"start":99.5,"end":103.58,"text":"and athletes need to spend a lot of time training to be good at a sport.","coverage":1},{"start":104.98,"end":111.08,"text":"So big companies might give money to sports teams and individual athletes to help them train.","coverage":1},{"start":111.78,"end":113.26,"text":"In some competitions,","coverage":1},{"start":113.64,"end":114.46,"text":"like the Olympics,","coverage":1},{"start":115.02,"end":118.06,"text":"there are both professional players and amateurs,","coverage":1},{"start":118.76,"end":123.32,"text":"you know, people who do the sport as a hobby and not as a job.","coverage":1},{"start":124.24,"end":127.2,"text":"I think both should be able to get support from companies.","coverage":1},{"start":128.22,"end":129.5,"text":"Look at Maria Sakary.","coverage":1},{"start":130.32,"end":137.7,"text":"She's a Greek tennis player who is paid money by a clothing company to wear their clothes and be in their adverts.","coverage":1},{"start":138.6,"end":140.24,"text":"Other companies support her too.","coverage":1},{"start":140.24,"end":142.74,"text":"Without all the help from companies,","coverage":1},{"start":143.18,"end":147.02,"text":"she might not have enough money to play tennis as her job.","coverage":1},{"start":147.92,"end":152.42,"text":"Having that time and money allows her to be such a good tennis player.","coverage":1},{"start":153.28,"end":156.38,"text":"But when a big company pays a team or an athlete,","coverage":1},{"start":156.92,"end":159.72,"text":"it makes them wear the company name and designs,","coverage":1},{"start":160.16,"end":162.06,"text":"and they sign contracts.","coverage":1},{"start":162.86,"end":166.44,"text":"Isn't that really like being an employee and working for a company?","coverage":1},{"start":167.14,"end":171,"text":"To me, these athletes work in advertising and marketing.","coverage":1},{"start":172.04,"end":173.04,"text":"You have a point,","coverage":1},{"start":173.7,"end":176.1,"text":"but if the athletes don't get good coaching,","coverage":1},{"start":176.64,"end":180.34,"text":"they might not score a lot of points and do well in competitions.","coverage":1},{"start":181.16,"end":182.18,"text":"If that happens,","coverage":1},{"start":182.6,"end":187.06,"text":"they can lose their chance to make a lot of money after the competitions are over.","coverage":1},{"start":187.82,"end":188.6,"text":"And actually,","coverage":1},{"start":189.1,"end":194.68,"text":"only about five % of Olympic athletes get money from companies to be in adverts.","coverage":1},{"start":195.74,"end":197.24,"text":"That doesn't sound fair.","coverage":1},{"start":198.02,"end":201.2,"text":"Shouldn't countries pay their own athletes a salary to train?","coverage":1},{"start":202.26,"end":204.68,"text":"After all, they do represent the countries.","coverage":1},{"start":205.66,"end":210.94,"text":"I read that in the UK, the government pays the country's Olympic athletes to train,","coverage":1},{"start":211.3,"end":214.32,"text":"so there is less pressure there to get money from a company.","coverage":1},{"start":215.44,"end":216.02,"text":"Also,","coverage":1},{"start":216.4,"end":221.44,"text":"there are prizes for all the competitions, and sometimes that gives them extra money.","coverage":1},{"start":222.38,"end":222.82,"text":"Well,","coverage":1},{"start":223.32,"end":226.76,"text":"a lot of countries can't pay the costs for training athletes.","coverage":1},{"start":227.56,"end":228.32,"text":"And of course,","coverage":1},{"start":228.74,"end":232.72,"text":"the countries with lots of money can train their athletes very well.","coverage":1},{"start":233.52,"end":235.86,"text":"If companies are supporting lots of athletes,","coverage":1},{"start":236.5,"end":239.04,"text":"more people can participate in competitions.","coverage":1},{"start":240.28,"end":245.78,"text":"Still, I think all this money takes something away from the Olympics and other sporting events.","coverage":1},{"start":246.96,"end":249.54,"text":"We see adverts almost everywhere.","coverage":1},{"start":250.34,"end":255.78,"text":"But being in an advert is a great opportunity for the athlete and the business.","coverage":1},{"start":256.56,"end":266.28,"text":"If an athlete lets his or her face be on a cereal box or wears some clothing with a company's name on it, people will probably buy the product.","coverage":1},{"start":266.88,"end":268.44,"text":"So it's good for the company,","coverage":1},{"start":268.92,"end":271.1,"text":"and the athlete gets more money to train.","coverage":1},{"start":272.1,"end":280.98,"text":"I also think that all the adverts at big competitions like the Olympics or the World Cup help lower the ticket prices for fans,","coverage":1},{"start":281.56,"end":284.12,"text":"so the competitions don't have to charge so much.","coverage":1},{"start":284.98,"end":286.18,"text":"It's good for everyone.","coverage":1},{"start":287.22,"end":287.74,"text":"Hmm,","coverage":1},{"start":288.56,"end":291.94,"text":"I'm not sure if I agree with you, but I understand your point.","coverage":1}],"file":"64ea1af6d6d04e42e0b1.js","track":0,"media":"../assets/media/d03378d2ce6264fc09340a9807bf5ddb3bdb18eab63cfbca14309bd008cc5b01.mp3"}],"../assets/media/a5448c7ab9134941a3c4074def61321f3542345d16240438cdbb018cd56dd37c.mp3":[{"id":"PPT_a5448c7ab9134941","audioId":"PPT_a5448c7ab9134941","title":"Book 2 · Unit 5 · LS · LISTENING 1","subtitle":"LISTENING 1 · source slide 67","duration":94.93,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.28,"text":"five .three","coverage":1},{"start":3.72,"end":4.68,"text":"one","coverage":1},{"start":5.22,"end":6.12,"text":"Now,","coverage":1},{"start":6.66,"end":13.18,"text":"chess boxing is a new type of sport where the players do both activities.","coverage":1},{"start":14.12,"end":15.6,"text":"They start with boxing,","coverage":1},{"start":15.96,"end":16.38,"text":"sorry,","coverage":1},{"start":16.9,"end":18.34,"text":"I mean chess,","coverage":1},{"start":18.8,"end":20.72,"text":"and then do some boxing,","coverage":1},{"start":21.22,"end":26.44,"text":"and they continue doing each activity back and forth, alternating.","coverage":1},{"start":28.54,"end":29.5,"text":"two","coverage":1},{"start":30.7,"end":31.66,"text":"Next,","coverage":1},{"start":32.16,"end":35.66,"text":"I'd like to talk about the Moroccan desert foot race,","coverage":1},{"start":36.14,"end":40.1,"text":"which is also called the marathon des Sables,","coverage":1},{"start":40.68,"end":43.12,"text":"or the Tahara marathon.","coverage":1},{"start":44.18,"end":48.14,"text":"This race is held every year over a week,","coverage":1},{"start":48.66,"end":49.5,"text":"or rather,","coverage":1},{"start":50.12,"end":51.26,"text":"over six days.","coverage":1},{"start":53.44,"end":54.4,"text":"three","coverage":1},{"start":55.46,"end":56.16,"text":"Finally,","coverage":1},{"start":56.86,"end":60.16,"text":"I'd like to look at Sepak Takraw.","coverage":1},{"start":61.06,"end":67.12,"text":"This is a type of volleyball and is very popular in Southeast Asia.","coverage":1},{"start":68.06,"end":70.86,"text":"The players use a different kind of ball,","coverage":1},{"start":71.52,"end":73.96,"text":"and they can use their feet to kick the ball,","coverage":1},{"start":74.38,"end":76.94,"text":"or hit it with their knees, chest,","coverage":1},{"start":77.28,"end":77.82,"text":"or head.","coverage":1},{"start":77.82,"end":81.22,"text":"The sport began in Indonesia,","coverage":1},{"start":81.96,"end":82.52,"text":"and it,","coverage":1},{"start":82.94,"end":83.48,"text":"no,","coverage":1},{"start":83.9,"end":84.7,"text":"not Indonesia,","coverage":1},{"start":85.38,"end":87.54,"text":"it began in Malaysia,","coverage":1},{"start":88.58,"end":92.96,"text":"although it is also very popular in Thailand and Indonesia.","coverage":1}],"file":"d1e9d8578758a26a18ea.js","track":0,"media":"../assets/media/a5448c7ab9134941a3c4074def61321f3542345d16240438cdbb018cd56dd37c.mp3"}],"../assets/media/0b0a0f7cb6c818009fb1e42514698d0eb59bc8088517ec94f08e5174e501ac56.mp3":[{"id":"PPT_0b0a0f7cb6c81800","audioId":"PPT_0b0a0f7cb6c81800","title":"Book 2 · Unit 5 · LS · PREPARATION FOR SPEAKING","subtitle":"PREPARATION FOR SPEAKING · source slide 175","duration":34.17,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.92,"text":"five .six","coverage":1},{"start":3.54,"end":4.38,"text":"one.","coverage":1},{"start":5.52,"end":11.6,"text":"I think there is definitely more marketing and business in sport than ever before.","coverage":1},{"start":13.9,"end":14.74,"text":"two.","coverage":1},{"start":15.92,"end":16.54,"text":"And actually,","coverage":1},{"start":16.92,"end":22.8,"text":"only about five % of Olympic athletes get money from big companies to be in adverts.","coverage":1},{"start":25.16,"end":25.88,"text":"three.","coverage":1},{"start":27.26,"end":32.34,"text":"And of course, the countries with lots of money can train their athletes very well.","coverage":1}],"file":"e35974f9fc4cda6f3950.js","track":0,"media":"../assets/media/0b0a0f7cb6c818009fb1e42514698d0eb59bc8088517ec94f08e5174e501ac56.mp3"}]};
window.SCHOOL_SOURCE_ANSWERS=[{"text":"1 Can you name some popular board games?Possible answers: chess, Go, Monopoly and draughts.","slide":4,"shape":"7","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"2 Why do people like to play games?Possible answer: Games are fun, help people relax and give friends something to do together.","slide":4,"shape":"17","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"3 How do people usually feel when they win or lose a game?Possible answer: Winners often feel happy or proud. Losing can be disappointing,but players may still enjoy the game.","slide":4,"shape":"5","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"1 You need to think a lot when you play chess.True. You need to think a lot when you play chess.","slide":11,"shape":"7","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"2 Computers can play chess better than humans.True in this example. Computers can play chess better than humans.","slide":11,"shape":"17","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"3 It doesn’t take long to play a game of chess.False. It can take a long time to play a game of chess.","slide":11,"shape":"5","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"1  Deep Blue was built by IBM.","slide":14,"shape":"8","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"2  A person with exceptional chess ability can be called a genius.","slide":14,"shape":"9","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"3  Moving a piece to a new position is a move.","slide":14,"shape":"10","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"4  A player may try to trick an opponent into making a mistake.","slide":14,"shape":"11","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"5  Kasparov could not escape from the difficult position.","slide":14,"shape":"12","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"1  Humans began playing chess nearly 500 years ago. False. Humans began playing chess nearly 1,500 years ago.","slide":17,"shape":"6","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"2  Garry Kasparov played a famous chess match against a child. False. Garry Kasparov played a famous chess match against an IBM supercomputer, Deep Blue.","slide":17,"shape":"7","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"3  A computer can only calculate numbers to play chess. True. A computer can only calculate numbers to play chess.","slide":17,"shape":"8","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"4  An engineer moved the chess pieces. True. An engineer moved the chess pieces.","slide":17,"shape":"9","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"5  A genius like Kasparov can think about three moves a minute. False. A genius like Kasparov can think about three moves a second.","slide":17,"shape":"10","bookPage":"104"},{"text":"First game\nSecond game\na Garry Kasparov played the game very well.\nb It seemed like the computer was thinking.\nd In the end, the computer lost.\nc The computer did not make a move for 15 minutes.\ne The game took nearly four hours.\nf Kasparov tried to trick the computer.","slide":21,"shape":"12","bookPage":"105"},{"text":"Main skillsMaths, planning and thinking.","slide":23,"shape":"13","bookPage":"105"},{"text":"Other skillsPossible answer: Listening helps when learning from a coach, but teamwork is not a central part of an individual chess game.","slide":23,"shape":"15","bookPage":"105"},{"text":"1 What other games can humans play against or with computers?Possible answers: cards, football games and racing games.","slide":25,"shape":"7","bookPage":"105"},{"text":"2 Is it better to play games against a human or a computer? Why?Possible answer: I prefer a human opponent because we can talk about the game afterwards. A computer is useful when nobody else is available.","slide":25,"shape":"17","bookPage":"105"},{"text":"3 Esports are played on computers. In what ways are they similar to sports?Possible answer: Players practise skills, follow rules and compete. Some games require teamwork.","slide":25,"shape":"5","bookPage":"105"},{"text":"4 How can esports help you learn to play and get better at games or sports?Possible answer: I can practise making decisions and study my mistakes by replaying a game.","slide":26,"shape":"10","bookPage":"105"},{"text":"1 The teacher’s name isn’t Mr Rosso. It’s Mr Rosson.","slide":28,"shape":"7","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"2 I had a golf lesson, not a tennis lesson.","slide":28,"shape":"16","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"3 The match is at 6:00 tonight, not 6:30, so don’t be late.","slide":28,"shape":"5","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"4 Yasmin doesn’t do Drama classes; she does Gymnastics classes.","slide":29,"shape":"5","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"5 The competition will be in Colombia, not in Brazil.","slide":29,"shape":"13","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"1 Which words does the speaker stress most strongly in each sentence?Both the incorrect and correct information: Rosso / Rosson; golf / tennis; 6:00 / 6:30; Drama / Gymnastics; Colombia / Brazil.","slide":32,"shape":"14","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"2 Does the intonation go up or down at the end of the sentence?It goes down.","slide":32,"shape":"16","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"1 The most popular sport in my country is basketball.The most popular sport in my country isn’t basketball. It’s cricket.","slide":34,"shape":"16","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"2 My favourite sport is bowling.My favourite sport isn’t bowling. It’s tennis.","slide":34,"shape":"18","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"3 Work with a partner. Correct the sentences by changing the underlined words to make them true, or true for you. Then compare your sentences.Formula One drivers race in cars, not on motorbikes.","slide":34,"shape":"6","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"4 We use a football to play golf.We use a golf ball, not a football, to play golf.","slide":35,"shape":"13","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"5 I study Sports Science.I don’t study Sports Science. I study Business.","slide":35,"shape":"15","bookPage":"106"},{"text":"competeTo do an activity with other people and try to do better than them.","slide":46,"shape":"15","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"championSomebody who wins a competition.","slide":46,"shape":"17","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"hitTo touch something quickly and forcefully with your hand or an object.","slide":46,"shape":"6","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"kickTo hit something with your foot.","slide":47,"shape":"15","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"strongPhysically powerful.","slide":47,"shape":"17","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"intelligentAble to understand and learn well.","slide":47,"shape":"6","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"1 Do you, or would you like to, do esports? Why / Why not?Possible answer: I would like to try esports because I enjoy computer games and team competitions.","slide":49,"shape":"7","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"2 What sports do you want to try? Why?Possible answer: I want to try archery because it requires concentration.","slide":49,"shape":"17","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"3 Are there some sports that you don’t like? Why?Possible answer: I don’t like boxing because I don’t want to be hit.","slide":49,"shape":"5","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"1 This report is mainly about unusual sports and … a where people do them. b how people do them.Answer: b — how people do them.","slide":52,"shape":"7","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"2 Some of these sports combine … a team and individual sports. b different sports activities and equipment.Answer: b — different sports activities and equipment.","slide":52,"shape":"18","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"3 The speaker talks about … a how to become a champion in each sport. b what intelligent players do in some sports.Answer: b — what intelligent players do in some sports.","slide":52,"shape":"20","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"4 The speaker doesn’t discuss … a the difficulties of the Sahara Marathon. b how long the Sahara Marathon is.Answer: a — the difficulties of the Sahara Marathon.","slide":53,"shape":"14","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"5 Sepak takraw is often played by … a volleyball teams. b schoolchildren.Answer: b — schoolchildren.","slide":53,"shape":"16","bookPage":"107"},{"text":"Unusual sports\nNotes\nChess\n(1) intelligent players need to think carefully.\nBoxing\nStrong boxers have to (2) hit each other.\nTwo activities\nFirst (3) chess, then (4) boxing.\nBenefit\nBoth mental and physical activity.","slide":59,"shape":"15","bookPage":"108"},{"text":"Unusual sports\nNotes\nEquipment\nUse golf clubs and (5) (soft) tennis balls.\nLocation\nPlay in the (6) street, not on a golf course.\nAdvantages\nDon’t need to go anywhere special or need much (7) money to play.\nDisadvantage\nMight (8) break something if you hit the ball too hard.","slide":60,"shape":"16","bookPage":"108"},{"text":"Unusual sports\nNotes\nDuration\nIt happens over (9) six days.\nLongest day\n92 kilometres.\nBenefit\nYou can say you have won the (10) hardest race in the world.","slide":61,"shape":"16","bookPage":"108"},{"text":"Unusual sports\nNotes\nType of sport\nA type of volleyball.\nEquipment and body parts\nPlayers use different balls and use (11) feet, knees, chest or (12) head.\nOrigin and popularity\nStarted in (13) Malaysia; popular in Southeast Asia, Thailand and Indonesia.\nBenefit\nGets children to play sports because it is played in (14) schools in many countries.","slide":62,"shape":"15","bookPage":"108"},{"text":"1 In chess boxing, they begin with chess and then switch.","slide":68,"shape":"7","bookPage":"108"},{"text":"2 The Sahara Marathon happens over six days in Morocco.","slide":68,"shape":"19","bookPage":"108"},{"text":"3 Sepak takraw began in Malaysia and is very popular.","slide":68,"shape":"21","bookPage":"108"},{"text":"1. Chess players need to think very carefully.","slide":71,"shape":"5","bookPage":null},{"text":"11. What is more important in boxing, according to the speaker?\nA. Speed of movement\nB. Physical strength\nC. Careful planning","slide":71,"shape":"8","bookPage":null},{"text":"1 Fans enjoy watching their favourite teams do sports. a coaches who work with teams b people who like famous groups or people c people on TV who talk about games and matchesAnswer: b — people who like famous groups or people","slide":86,"shape":"5","bookPage":"113"},{"text":"2 Some people are paid a salary for a full-time job. They aren’t paid by the hour. a the things you like about your job b the good things about your job c the money you get from your jobAnswer: c — the money you get from your job","slide":86,"shape":"16","bookPage":"113"},{"text":"3 Some big companies support players by giving them clothing to wear. a help or care for somebody b prepare somebody c get money from somebodyAnswer: a — help or care for somebody","slide":87,"shape":"5","bookPage":"113"},{"text":"4 Ticket sellers charge people a lot of money to go to a popular match. a sell tickets to people b ask people to pay for something c give money to workersAnswer: b — ask people to pay for something","slide":87,"shape":"16","bookPage":"113"},{"text":"5 Every year, there are football competitions like the World Cup and the Copa del Rey. a games that players like b games that many fans go to c games that people try to winAnswer: c — games that people try to win","slide":88,"shape":"5","bookPage":"113"},{"text":"6 The prize in the golf competition is money and a silver cup. a something that a player gets when they win b something that a player gets for being in a competition c something that a person pays to be in a competitionAnswer: a — something that a player gets when they win","slide":88,"shape":"13","bookPage":"113"},{"text":"7 In football, the team that scores more goals wins. a is the best b gets points in a game c hits a ballAnswer: b — gets points in a game","slide":89,"shape":"5","bookPage":"113"},{"text":"8 The cost of buying a sports team is millions of pounds. a the salary for a sports team b how many fans a team has c how much money you need to buy somethingAnswer: c — how much money you need to buy something","slide":89,"shape":"13","bookPage":"113"},{"text":"Exercise 2.1 Obviously, athletes should be able to take money from companies for support.Andre.","slide":92,"shape":"7","bookPage":"114"},{"text":"Exercise 2.2 Actually, seeing adverts everywhere at the Olympics is quite annoying.Ian.","slide":92,"shape":"18","bookPage":"114"},{"text":"Exercise 3.1 What bias does Ian, the fan, have?He is biased against companies paying athletes because he is a sports fan.","slide":92,"shape":"20","bookPage":"114"},{"text":"Exercise 3.2 What bias does Andre, the former sportsperson, have?He is biased in favour of companies paying athletes because he has been a sportsperson.","slide":93,"shape":"11","bookPage":"114"},{"text":"Agree\nDisagree\nReason: without (1) sport, athletes have no job.Support: athletes can’t live, work and pay for training; cost of coaching is really high.\nReason: all athletes are interested in making huge (7) amounts of money.Support: more marketing than ever.","slide":99,"shape":"15","bookPage":"114"},{"text":"Agree\nDisagree\nReason: athletes need good coaching.Support: don’t do well in competitions, lose chance to (2) make money; only (3) 5% of Olympic athletes get money from companies.\nReason: athletes are like (8) employees.Support: get paid to wear companies’ names on clothing; (9) sign contracts.","slide":100,"shape":"16","bookPage":"114"},{"text":"Agree\nDisagree\nReason: a lot of countries can’t pay the costs for (4) training.Support: more people can (5) participate.\nReason: athletes should represent their (10) countries.Support: there would be less pressure to get money from a company.","slide":101,"shape":"16","bookPage":"114"},{"text":"Agree\nDisagree\nReason: good for everyone — athletes, (6) companies, fans.Support: everyone gets moneyor lower costs.\nReason: all the money takes away from Olympics.Support: see (11) adverts everywhere.","slide":102,"shape":"15","bookPage":"114"},{"text":"1  It seems like the athletes are more interested in making money than in representing\ntheir countries. O — opinion","slide":108,"shape":"7","bookPage":"115"},{"text":"2  Without all the help from companies, she might not have enough money to play tennis\nas her ‘job’. O — opinion","slide":108,"shape":"8","bookPage":"115"},{"text":"3  And actually, only about 5% of Olympic athletes get money from big companies to be\nin adverts. S — support","slide":108,"shape":"9","bookPage":"115"},{"text":"4  I read that in the UK, the government pays the country’s Olympic athletes to train, so\nthere is less pressure there to get money from a company. S — support","slide":108,"shape":"10","bookPage":"115"},{"text":"1 It seems like the athletes are more interested in making money than in representing their countries.Possible answer: Ian thinks athletes focus on money because, on his US holiday, he repeatedly saw famous athletes in adverts.","slide":110,"shape":"14","bookPage":"115"},{"text":"2 Without all the help from companies, she might not have enough money to play tennis as her ‘job’.Possible answer: Andre thinks company support helps Maria Sakkari play professionally because sponsors pay her to wear their clothing and appear in adverts.","slide":111,"shape":"13","bookPage":"115"},{"text":"New sentence 1Possible answer: I think teamwork matters because our team improved after we started practising passes together.","slide":111,"shape":"15","bookPage":"115"},{"text":"New sentence 2Possible answer: I think regular practice is helpful because I made fewer serving mistakes after practising each week.","slide":112,"shape":"14","bookPage":"115"},{"text":"1 If your team wins the game, the other team loses.","slide":121,"shape":"11","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"2 If chess players are intelligent, they plan their moves.","slide":121,"shape":"16","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"3 You hit the ball with a bat if you play cricket.","slide":121,"shape":"5","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"4 My team won’t be the champions if they don’t win the match on Monday.","slide":121,"shape":"7","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"5 My feet will hurt if I compete in another marathon.","slide":121,"shape":"9","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"6 If you exercise often, you will be strong.","slide":122,"shape":"15","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"1 If it rains hard during the match tomorrow, they will cancel it.","slide":124,"shape":"11","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"2 You hit a soft tennis ball if you play urban golf.","slide":124,"shape":"16","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"3 If you play volleyball, the team has six players.","slide":124,"shape":"5","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"4 If he hits hard, he might win the boxing match.","slide":124,"shape":"7","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"5 If we are late, we may miss the game.","slide":124,"shape":"9","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"6 If you don’t buy a ticket, you can’t watch the game.","slide":125,"shape":"15","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"1 Possible answer: If I play my favourite sport, I feel relaxed afterwards.","slide":127,"shape":"16","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"2 Possible answer: If I have free time in the evening, I usually go swimming.","slide":127,"shape":"18","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"3 Possible answer: I will try archery if I get a chance to try a new sport next year.","slide":128,"shape":"10","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"4 Possible answer: If my family wants to do something interesting during our next holiday, we might try sailing.","slide":128,"shape":"12","bookPage":"111"},{"text":"1 Football is very popular as a sport all over the world.","slide":134,"shape":"16","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"2 It isn’t very expensive to watch local sports games.","slide":134,"shape":"18","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"3 The team played extremely well – they were the champions!","slide":135,"shape":"16","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"4 Mehmet ran very quickly and finished in second place in the race.","slide":135,"shape":"18","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"5 The coach made us exercise really hard.","slide":136,"shape":"11","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"6 Chess is a fairly slow game because the players must plan their moves.","slide":136,"shape":"13","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"7 Sophia didn’t sleep well last night. She didn’t play in the match this afternoon because she was too tired.","slide":136,"shape":"6","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"DegreePossible answer: Fairly quickly suggests a moderate speed; very quickly suggests a high speed.","slide":139,"shape":"13","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"TooPossible answer: Too tired means more tired than is acceptable for an activity.Very tired simply describes a high degree of tiredness.","slide":139,"shape":"15","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"1 What sports or activities are you good at?Possible answer: I play badminton quite well.","slide":141,"shape":"7","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"2 Are there any sports or activities that you are not very good at? Which ones?Possible answer: I’m not very good at skiing because I haven’t practised much.","slide":141,"shape":"17","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"3 Which subjects or topics are you extremely interested in? Why?Possible answer: I’m extremely interested in biology because I enjoy learning about animals.","slide":141,"shape":"5","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"4 What happened the last time you arrived too late for something?Possible answer: I arrived too late for a match and missed the first goal.","slide":142,"shape":"5","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"5 What things do you think are fairly boring in your job or studies?Possible answer: I find copying long lists fairly boring.","slide":142,"shape":"14","bookPage":"112"},{"text":"If I finish early, I will watch the match.","slide":147,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"If our team wins, we will play in the final.","slide":147,"shape":"9","bookPage":null},{"text":"We have a plan for tomorrow's practice. If it rains, we will use the sports hall. The hall has an indoor court. We can practise on that court.","slide":148,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"I would like to watch the school final. The final is at the local stadium. That stadium has only a few seats left. I will book one of those seats today.","slide":149,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"A player is kicking a football on a grass field. There is a goal behind him.","slide":150,"shape":"7","bookPage":null},{"text":"If the ball goes into the goal, the player may score. His teammates may celebrate.","slide":150,"shape":"10","bookPage":null},{"text":"1. Chess players are described as intelligent because the game requires careful thought.","slide":155,"shape":"5","bookPage":null},{"text":"11. What does the speaker say about boxing despite its protective equipment?\nA. It is still difficult.\nB. It needs less strength.\nC. It has become easier to win.","slide":155,"shape":"8","bookPage":null},{"text":"1. Chess boxing combines a board game with a physical contest.\nAnswer: TRUE","slide":158,"shape":"5","bookPage":null},{"text":"11. Careful urban golfers are trying to avoid breaking things.\nAnswer: TRUE","slide":158,"shape":"8","bookPage":null},{"text":"The new course is rather challenging.","slide":166,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"We will enter the competition if we have enough players.","slide":166,"shape":"9","bookPage":null},{"text":"We are looking for an affordable way to play. The club offers a group discount. That discount applies to six people. If we find two more friends, we can use it.","slide":167,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"Our last match showed us what to work on. We lost the ball when passing. Those missed passes stopped our attacks. We will practise passing if the court is free tomorrow.","slide":168,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"A man is holding a basketball on an outdoor court. The hoop is behind him. If a friend joins him, they can practise passing.","slide":169,"shape":"7","bookPage":null},{"text":"If the player scores, his team may feel more confident. The other team may then try to score too. The match could become more exciting.","slide":170,"shape":"7","bookPage":null},{"text":"1 What are some reasons for an athlete to participate in a big sports competition like the Olympics or the World Cup?Possible answers: to become a champion, compete with other excellent athletes and improve at their sport.","slide":173,"shape":"5","bookPage":"116"},{"text":"2 Why do companies want to support athletes at big competitions?Possible answer: Famous athletes attract attention to the company and its products.","slide":173,"shape":"17","bookPage":"116"},{"text":"3 What are two reasons why some fans don’t like the idea of companies supporting athletes?Possible answers: They think sport should be about competition rather than money; they dislike athletes advertising for big companies.","slide":174,"shape":"16","bookPage":"116"},{"text":"6  Because of television, sports organizations get a lot of money. It is right that players\nhave high salaries. E — enough","slide":177,"shape":"7","bookPage":"117"},{"text":"4  Sports players create a lot of money for their teams and clubs, so they should be paid\nwell. E — enough","slide":177,"shape":"12","bookPage":"117"},{"text":"5  It takes years of hard work to become excellent at a sport — so players who have\ntrained hard should be rewarded. E — enough","slide":177,"shape":"13","bookPage":"117"},{"text":"2 Athletes become more professional when they get paid more.Possible answer: I don’t think number 2 gives a reason why more pay makes an athlete more professional. It needs support, such as how the money pays for specialist training.","slide":179,"shape":"13","bookPage":"117"},{"text":"3 Sports are not really that important and so people should not be paid a lot to play them.Possible answer: Number 3 does not explain why sport is unimportant. I think sport can help people stay healthy.","slide":179,"shape":"15","bookPage":"117"},{"text":"Role and positionAs a parent, I think athletes can deserve extremely large amounts of money when their work creates great value.","slide":188,"shape":"16","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"Reason 1: reward years of trainingAndre says many athletes devote their whole lives to training. Successful athletes have invested years in developing rare skills.","slide":188,"shape":"18","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"Reason 2: athletes create valueAndre explains that famous athletes can help companies sell products. If their work brings in more money, high pay can be fair.","slide":189,"shape":"13","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"Reason 3: a career can be shortAn athlete may earn most of their career income during a short period. High pay during those years can help support life after sport.","slide":189,"shape":"15","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"An opposing viewA charity worker may say the money should buy food and medicine. I agree these needs matter; athletes could donate part of their earnings.","slide":190,"shape":"14","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"Possible argument: People in sports should get paid extremely large amounts of money.","slide":191,"shape":"7","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"Reason 1Reward years of training","slide":191,"shape":"12","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"SupportAthletes devote years to developing rare skills.","slide":191,"shape":"15","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"Reason 2Athletes create value","slide":191,"shape":"18","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"SupportFamous athletes help companies sell products.","slide":191,"shape":"21","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"Reason 3Careers can be short","slide":191,"shape":"24","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"SupportHigh pay can help support life after sport.","slide":191,"shape":"27","bookPage":"118"},{"text":"1  I think there is definitely more marketing and business in sport than ever before.","slide":194,"shape":"7","bookPage":"119"},{"text":"2  And actually, only about 5% of Olympic athletes get money from big companies to\nbe in adverts.","slide":194,"shape":"8","bookPage":"119"},{"text":"3  And of course, the countries with lots of money can train their athletes very well.","slide":194,"shape":"9","bookPage":"119"},{"text":"a Possible answer: Actually, an athlete can need financial support even without being famous.","slide":197,"shape":"16","bookPage":"119"},{"text":"b Possible answer: Of course, we should also consider the fans’ experience.","slide":197,"shape":"18","bookPage":"119"},{"text":"c Possible answer: Players definitely need time to train.","slide":198,"shape":"10","bookPage":"119"},{"text":"d Possible answer: Obviously, we need evidence before deciding that a salary is too high.","slide":198,"shape":"12","bookPage":"119"},{"text":"1 The photo on page 119 shows the sport of surfing. In this sport, the wave gets a 1 to 10 score, and the surfers get points for the types of moves they do and how difficult those moves are. Why do you think surfing has these rules?Possible answer: A: I think the rules help compare performances on different waves.B: Can you give more detail?A: More difficult moves can receive more points.","slide":202,"shape":"13","bookPage":"120"},{"text":"2 Why do you think it’s important to have rules in sports? Give support for your reasons. Are there any sport rules that you would change?Possible answer: A: Rules help players know how points are scored and who has won.B: Could you give an example?A: In a race, everyone needs the same agreed start and finish.","slide":203,"shape":"13","bookPage":"120"},{"text":"1 (c) I: What was your plan today?","slide":205,"shape":"15","bookPage":"120"},{"text":"2 (e) C: My plan was to ride some good waves and have fun.","slide":205,"shape":"17","bookPage":"120"},{"text":"3 (d) I: What’s a good wave? Can you give some more detail?","slide":205,"shape":"6","bookPage":"120"},{"text":"4 (b) C: Well, today, the waves were 4.5 metres high. You need to be strong to ride those waves. We wanted to give everybody a good show!","slide":205,"shape":"8","bookPage":"120"},{"text":"1 (f) I: Surfing is an Olympic sport. But people say it’s dangerous. Do you agree?","slide":208,"shape":"15","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"2 (b) C: Obviously, as a surfer, I agree that it might be dangerous if the waves are extremely big. But actually, it’s usually pretty safe. That’s one reason why it’s popular.","slide":208,"shape":"17","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"3 (c) I: Can you explain what you mean by that? Why do people want to do this sport?","slide":208,"shape":"6","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"5 (f) I: That’s really big! But what do you mean by giving a good show?","slide":209,"shape":"15","bookPage":"120"},{"text":"6 (a) C: Well, in surfing, it’s important to do different moves, not the same ones again and again …","slide":209,"shape":"17","bookPage":"120"},{"text":"4 (e) C: Sure. People can ride small waves and have a lot of fun. And you don’t need an expensive board to ride.","slide":210,"shape":"15","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"5 (d) I: It’s great that it can be easy and cheap. Can you give some examples of the excitement of surfing?","slide":210,"shape":"17","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"6 (a) C: Definitely! One example of the excitement of surfing is watching the surfers’ amazing moves …","slide":210,"shape":"6","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"Can you give some more detail?Possible alternatives: Could you give an example? Can you explain what you mean?","slide":213,"shape":"13","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"What do you mean by …?Possible alternatives: I’m sorry, I don’t understand. I’m afraid I didn’t get that.","slide":213,"shape":"15","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"I: Can you explain what you mean by that? Why do people want to do this sport?","slide":217,"shape":"12","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"I: It’s great that it can be easy and cheap. Can you give some examples of the excitement of surfing?","slide":217,"shape":"14","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"C: Definitely! One example of the excitement of surfing is watching the surfers’ amazing moves …","slide":217,"shape":"6","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"C: Obviously, as a surfer, I agree that it might be dangerous if the waves are extremely big. But actually, it’s usually pretty safe. That’s one reason why it’s popular.","slide":218,"shape":"13","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"Ask for moreCan you give more detail?","slide":220,"shape":"13","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"Emphasize a pointOf course, regular practice helps players improve.","slide":220,"shape":"15","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"1  Sorry, I didn’t follow what you said. DU — I don’t understand","slide":222,"shape":"6","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"2  Can you explain what you mean? EM — I want you to explain more","slide":222,"shape":"7","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"3  I’m afraid I didn’t get that. DU — I don’t understand","slide":222,"shape":"8","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"4  I’m sorry, but I don’t understand. DU — I don’t understand","slide":222,"shape":"9","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"5  Would you mind giving some examples? EM — I want you to explain more","slide":222,"shape":"10","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"Reason and supportA: Actually, football can be inexpensive. You can play an informal game with a ball and a suitable open space.","slide":225,"shape":"13","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"ClarificationB: Can you explain what you mean by inexpensive?A: I mean a casual game with friends, not joining a professional club or buying expensive equipment.","slide":225,"shape":"15","bookPage":"121"},{"text":"A — parentAs a parent, I think very successful athletes can deserve extremely high pay. If their skills create great value, they should share in it.","slide":231,"shape":"16","bookPage":"122"},{"text":"B — charity workerOf course, talent matters. But I oppose extremely high pay when people lack food and medicine. Some of that money could meet basic needs.","slide":231,"shape":"18","bookPage":"122"},{"text":"C — journalistCan you explain what you mean by “great value”? How could an athlete’s work justify such high pay?","slide":232,"shape":"13","bookPage":"122"},{"text":"D — footballerAndre says famous athletes can help sell products. If my work earns a club or sponsor a lot of money, I think a large share is fair. I could also support charities.","slide":232,"shape":"15","bookPage":"122"},{"text":"ClarificationA: I’m sorry, I don’t understand. What do you mean by supporting charities?D: For example, an athlete could donate some earnings to a local charity.","slide":233,"shape":"14","bookPage":"122"},{"text":"What do you mean by the entry fee?","slide":237,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"In other words, the money pays for the equipment.","slide":237,"shape":"9","bookPage":null},{"text":"The price makes more sense when we look at it closely. The club fee includes a weekly lesson. Each lesson is led by a coach. In other words, we are paying for regular coaching.","slide":238,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"Support does not always mean a large amount of money. A local shop helps our team. It lends us a van for away games. That transport is one useful example of support.","slide":239,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"I believe this player should practise regularly. The ball and open field give him space to improve his kick. Most importantly, practice can help him score more often. That is why training matters before a competition.","slide":240,"shape":"7","bookPage":null},{"text":"By support, I mean that teammates encourage the player during practice. The people in the picture can watch his kick and give useful advice. I am not saying that they guarantee a win. I mean that teamwork can help a player improve.","slide":241,"shape":"7","bookPage":null}];
